<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Scenario xmlns="http://adamantium/automation/scenario" Platforms="Linux MacOS" Description="The only window, minimized by its caption button, goes at once, with no input after the click: on Wayland the request waited in the connection's buffer for the next frame, and a minimized window draws none, so it stayed on screen until the pointer moved. The compositor's answer - the window no longer active - shows the request reached it; a Wayland window never learns it is minimized, so its activity is what tells. The main window alone, settled, its button invoked: another window drawing a frame, a frame still on its way, or the button drawn pressed would carry the request along. On Windows, MinimizeAtOnceWindows: there a window started from the background is not made active while someone works in another, so this one's first step could not be met.">
  <Wait Target="id=MainWindow" IsActive="True" />
  <WaitIdle />
  <Invoke Target="id=MainWindow/id=Minimize" />
  <Wait Target="id=MainWindow" IsActive="False" Timeout="2s" />
</Scenario>
